{
  "runId": "harness-memory-research-ms5ri7ot-lzrsqx",
  "workflowName": "harness-memory-research",
  "script": "export const meta = {\n  name: \"harness-memory-research\",\n  description: \"Prior-art research for cross-session memory + read-side protocol: local harness docs, local session storage layout, pi.dev/web ecosystem.\",\n  phases: [{ title: \"Research\" }],\n}\n\nconst CONTRACT = {\n  type: \"object\",\n  required: [\"outcome\", \"evidence\", \"changes\", \"decisions\", \"failures_risks\", \"new_tasks\", \"payload_json\"],\n  properties: {\n    outcome: { type: \"string\", description: \"What was found, 1-3 sentences\" },\n    evidence: { type: \"string\", description: \"Checkable proof: paths, URLs, excerpts\" },\n    changes: { type: \"array\", items: { type: \"string\" } },\n    decisions: { type: \"array\", items: { type: \"string\" } },\n    failures_risks: { type: \"array\", items: { type: \"string\" } },\n    new_tasks: { type: \"array\", items: { type: \"string\" } },\n    payload_json: { type: \"string\", description: \"JSON string with findings; {} if none\" },\n  },\n}\n\nphase(\"Research\")\nconst results = await parallel([\n  () => agent(`Read every Markdown file in /home/alex/Projects/pi-harness-config/docs (including the Agents/ subfolder). These are the operator's pi-harness engineering history. Extract everything relevant to: cross-session memory, session retrieval or indexing, compaction behavior, memory processors, and read-side protocols (agents consulting recorded decisions before acting). For each finding note source file and whether it is a decision, a measurement, or an open problem. Put findings in payload_json as {\"findings\":[{\"topic\",\"kind\",\"summary\",\"source\"}]}. Return the worker contract JSON with exactly: outcome, evidence, changes, decisions, failures_risks, new_tasks, payload_json — terse; transcripts stay in the journal, never in the result.`, { label: \"docs-history\", schema: CONTRACT }),\n  () => agent(`Map this pi harness's session storage to prepare a session-retrieval layer. Established fact to verify and detail: pi extensions support SessionStartEvent, SessionShutdownEvent, SessionCompactEvent, SessionBeforeCompactEvent — find exact event names, signatures, and payloads in /home/alex/.local/share/fnm/node-versions/v24.17.0/installation/lib/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/dist (grep the .d.ts files) so an extension can hook session end. Then inspect ~/.pi/agent/sessions/: how project dirs are named, file naming pattern, and JSONL record shapes (head one small file; identify message vs tool-call record types and where a session title or name lands, if anywhere). Also determine where context-mode's ctx_index persists its FTS5 store and how source labels work, so a session summary could be indexed and later found via ctx_search. Put findings in payload_json as {\"events\":[{\"name\",\"signature\",\"when\"}],\"sessions\":{\"dirPattern\",\"filePattern\",\"recordTypes\",\"titleField\"},\"ctxIndex\":{\"persistLocation\",\"labeling\"}}. Return the worker contract JSON with exactly: outcome, evidence, changes, decisions, failures_risks, new_tasks, payload_json — terse.`, { label: \"local-layout\", schema: CONTRACT }),\n  () => agent(`Web research: find existing solutions for cross-session agent memory in the pi coding-agent ecosystem and adjacent harnesses worth porting. Search the web (pi.dev, npm, GitHub) for: (1) pi packages or skills doing session memory, session search, or long-term agent memory — specifically whether a \"pi-hermes-memory\" package exists, what it does, and whether it is maintained; (2) Claude Code or other harness plugins for session-summary indexing and recall that are simple enough to port; (3) canonical agent-memory skill patterns (exclude heavy MCP memory servers unless tiny). Use whatever web search/fetch tools you have; if you have none, say so in failures_risks and put dated, low-confidence parametric knowledge in payload_json instead. Put findings in payload_json as {\"candidates\":[{\"name\",\"where\",\"what\",\"fit\",\"maturity\"}],\"recommendation\"}. Return the worker contract JSON with exactly: outcome, evidence, changes, decisions, failures_risks, new_tasks, payload_json — terse.`, { label: \"web-ecosystem\", schema: CONTRACT }),\n])\n\nconst names = [\"docs-history\", \"local-layout\", \"web-ecosystem\"]\nconst missing = []\nfor (let i = 0; i < results.length; i++) {\n  if (!results[i]) missing.push(names[i])\n}\nlog(\"research complete; missing coverage: \" + (missing.join(\", \") || \"none\"))\nreturn {\n  report: results.map((r, i) => `## ${names[i]}\\n` + (r ? r.outcome : \"MISSING COVERAGE\")).join(\"\\n\"),\n  docs_history: results[0] || null,\n  local_layout: results[1] || null,\n  web_ecosystem: results[2] || null,\n  incomplete: missing.length > 0,\n}",
