      "prompt": "Web research: find existing solutions for cross-session agent memory in the pi coding-agent ecosystem and adjacent harnesses worth porting. Search the web (pi.dev, npm, GitHub) for: (1) pi packages or skills doing session memory, session search, or long-term agent memory — specifically whether a \"pi-hermes-memory\" package exists, what it does, and whether it is maintained; (2) Claude Code or other harness plugins for session-summary indexing and recall that are simple enough to port; (3) canonical agent-memory skill patterns (exclude heavy MCP memory servers unless tiny). Use whatever web search/fetch tools you have; if you have none, say so in failures_risks and put dated, low-confidence parametric knowledge in payload_json instead. Put findings in payload_json as {\"candidates\":[{\"name\",\"where\",\"what\",\"fit\",\"maturity\"}],\"recommendation\"}. Return the worker contract JSON with exactly: outcome, evidence, changes, decisions, failures_risks, new_tasks, payload_json — terse.",
